# Call-site ledger of cachetools v8.0.0 (src/cachetools/, commit 1ce79efa552d1bdda70d144d401ef9105d999184).
# Written by hand from the source and Python semantics; judgements and statistics in cachetools.md.
# "Any package cache" below means an instance of Cache, FIFOCache, LFUCache, LRUCache, RRCache,
# TTLCache, TLRUCache or func._UnboundTTLCache. The private _TimedCache is not created by clients
# (cachetools.md, rule B1).

default reject cachetools._TimedCache._Timer.__getattr__: Python calls __getattr__ only when the normal lookup fails on a _Timer instance. The package loads attributes of a _Timer only in _Timer's own methods (self.__timer, self.__nesting, self.__time), and they are always set when read: __timer and __nesting in __init__ (copy and unpickling also call _Timer(timer), through __reduce__ at __init__.py:411), __time before __nesting first becomes non-zero (__init__.py:400-404). Special methods (__call__, __enter__, __exit__) are looked up on the type. Every other receiver at these sites is not a _Timer; at the explicit call getattr(self.__timer, name) (__init__.py:414) the receiver is the raw timer, which is never a _Timer: _Timer is private, the package creates one only in _TimedCache.__init__ (__init__.py:418) and through _Timer.__reduce__ (__init__.py:411), both times around the raw timer, and another cache's .timer is not a value for the timer parameter (cachetools.md, rules B1, B2, B3)

